WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.389 --> 00:00:16.050
next morning the whole school knew that Sara was in trouble.

2
00:00:16.971 --> 00:00:20.012
Everyone had heard that Miss Minchin wanted to fire Becky.

3
00:00:21.232 --> 00:00:25.374
But it was hard to find a good kitchen maid, so Becky didn't lose her job.

4
00:00:26.635 --> 00:00:29.156
Miss Minchin didn't send Sara away either.

5
00:00:30.536 --> 00:00:33.918
She had practical reasons for wanting to keep Sara at the school.

6
00:00:35.379 --> 00:00:39.802
Sara was teaching some of the other girls, and could perform difficult tasks.

7
00:00:41.083 --> 00:00:43.385
And Miss Minchin didn't have to pay her a cent.

8
00:00:44.886 --> 00:00:47.267
But Sara was given no food that day.

9
00:00:48.508 --> 00:00:50.970
As usual she was sent on many errands.

10
00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:54.852
She was even colder and wetter than the day before.

11
00:00:56.574 --> 00:01:00.076
At ten o'clock Sara wearily climbed the steps to the attic.

12
00:01:03.372 --> 00:01:07.055
"Oh, I hope the new things are still there," she whispered.

13
00:01:08.236 --> 00:01:10.637
She opened the door to her room and gasped.

14
00:01:12.258 --> 00:01:13.699
The fire was blazing.

15
00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.202
Supper for two was waiting on the table.

16
00:01:18.362 --> 00:01:21.184
A number of new things had been brought to the attic.

17
00:01:22.005 --> 00:01:25.047
The ugly mantel was hidden by a rich tapestry.

18
00:01:26.728 --> 00:01:32.032
Colorful fabrics and fans were tacked to the walls, and a long box rested on the floor.

19
00:01:32.936 --> 00:01:35.998
It was covered with a rug and cushions to make a sofa.

20
00:01:36.018 --> 00:01:39.821
"It's like I'm living in a fairy tale!"

21
00:01:40.242 --> 00:01:41.383
exclaimed Sara.

22
00:01:43.264 --> 00:01:46.586
She knocked on the wall, and Becky immediately appeared.

23
00:01:46.607 --> 00:01:48.408
"Oh my!"

24
00:01:49.048 --> 00:01:49.709
said Becky.

25
00:01:50.309 --> 00:01:52.191
Her eyes were wide with amazement.

26
00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:55.333
"Where does it all come from?"

27
00:01:55.353 --> 00:01:59.832
"I have no idea," said Sara.

28
00:01:59.852 --> 00:02:03.575
"But Miss Minchin must never find out what has been happening up here!"

29
00:02:06.698 --> 00:02:10.000
Sara discovered that she had a new mattress and pillows.

30
00:02:11.742 --> 00:02:14.784
Her old mattress and pillow were now on Becky's bed.

31
00:02:15.705 --> 00:02:17.646
So Becky's bed was now softer too.

32
00:02:18.887 --> 00:02:21.970
From that day on, life became more wonderful.

33
00:02:23.471 --> 00:02:26.053
Every night there was something new in Sara's room.

34
00:02:27.314 --> 00:02:29.256
Pictures covered the ugly walls.

35
00:02:30.072 --> 00:02:31.753
New pieces of furniture appeared.

36
00:02:32.914 --> 00:02:34.816
A bookshelf was filled with books.

37
00:02:37.037 --> 00:02:39.119
Miss Minchin was as harsh as ever.

38
00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:43.282
The cook and other servants were still rude to Sara.

39
00:02:44.623 --> 00:02:47.485
She was never allowed to speak to Ermengarde and Lottie.

40
00:02:48.786 --> 00:02:50.967
Lavinia continued to sneer at her.

41
00:02:51.848 --> 00:02:53.129
But Sara didn't mind.

42
00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:56.932
She had her lovely room to look forward to all day.

43
00:02:58.084 --> 00:03:00.305
She also had a hot meal every evening.

44
00:03:03.726 --> 00:03:07.568
And Sara enjoyed having a special secret to keep from Miss Minchin.

45
00:03:07.588 --> 00:03:10.349
"If you only knew!"

46
00:03:10.829 --> 00:03:13.130
she thought whenever Miss Minchin scolded her.

47
00:03:14.111 --> 00:03:17.372
But Miss Minchin had noticed something different about Sara.

48
00:03:17.392 --> 00:03:25.355
"Sara is looking remarkably well," Miss Minchin said to her sister one afternoon.

49
00:03:25.375 --> 00:03:31.477
"Yes, she used to look so starved," Miss Amelia replied.

50
00:03:31.497 --> 00:03:33.598
"Why do you say that?"

51
00:03:34.238 --> 00:03:35.418
snapped the headmistress.

52
00:03:35.438 --> 00:03:38.219
"She always had enough to eat."

53
00:03:38.239 --> 00:03:42.040
"Of course," Miss Amelia quickly agreed.

54
00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.341
She hated upsetting her sister.

55
00:03:44.361 --> 00:03:49.702
"There's something defiant about Sara," Miss Minchin went on.

56
00:03:49.722 --> 00:03:53.503
"She's still acting like she's a princess.

57
00:03:54.263 --> 00:03:55.764
I find that most annoying."

58
00:03:58.616 --> 00:04:01.018
One day a deliveryman came to the school.

59
00:04:01.978 --> 00:04:03.600
Sara was sent to open the door.

60
00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:06.562
The man handed her several packages.

61
00:04:08.303 --> 00:04:13.026
They were all addressed to "The Little Girl in the Right-hand Room in the Attic."

62
00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:18.430
Miss Minchin came downstairs as Sara was staring at the address labels.

63
00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:24.174
"Take those to the young lady to whom they belong," said the headmistress.

64
00:04:24.194 --> 00:04:27.336
"Don't just stand there staring at them."

65
00:04:29.148 --> 00:04:32.330
"But they're addressed to me," said Sara quietly.

66
00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:34.551
"To you?"

67
00:04:35.071 --> 00:04:36.292
exclaimed Miss Minchin.

68
00:04:36.312 --> 00:04:39.234
"Well then, open them right now!"

69
00:04:39.254 --> 00:04:43.176
"I don't know where they came from," Sara said.

70
00:04:45.157 --> 00:04:53.622
She opened the packages and found all kinds of beautiful, warm clothing—shoes, stockings, gloves, and a nice hat.

71
00:04:54.762 --> 00:04:57.184
There was even an umbrella and a winter coat.

72
00:04:58.988 --> 00:05:02.430
Pinned to the coat was a note: To be worn every day.

73
00:05:03.151 --> 00:05:05.192
Will be replaced when necessary.

74
00:05:06.713 --> 00:05:09.595
Miss Minchin was quite upset when she saw the clothing.

75
00:05:10.556 --> 00:05:12.777
Did Sara have a relative looking out for her?

76
00:05:13.758 --> 00:05:16.840
What if this person discovered how poorly Sara had been treated?

77
00:05:17.821 --> 00:05:19.742
He would be angry with Miss Minchin.

78
00:05:19.762 --> 00:05:25.366
"Well," she said in a voice that was softer than her usual one with Sara.

79
00:05:25.386 --> 00:05:28.608
"Someone has been very kind to you.

80
00:05:29.652 --> 00:05:31.833
You might as well change into your new clothes.

81
00:05:33.033 --> 00:05:37.314
After you are dressed, you may come downstairs and learn your lessons in the schoolroom.

82
00:05:38.435 --> 00:05:41.035
There's no need to do any more errands today."

83
00:05:43.076 --> 00:05:47.917
When Sara entered the schoolroom thirty minutes later, the girls whispered and stared.

84
00:05:49.858 --> 00:05:53.959
Sara was dressed in a beautiful dress and she wore a ribbon in her hair.

85
00:05:55.479 --> 00:05:58.880
She looked just like the old Sara.

86
00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:00.402
Jessie elbowed Lavinia.

87
00:06:00.422 --> 00:06:02.746
"Look at Princess Sara!"

88
00:06:02.766 --> 00:06:08.314
"Come sit here by me, Sara," Miss Minchin said.

89
00:06:09.295 --> 00:06:12.239
Sara went to her old seat of honor and sat down.

90
00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:15.464
Then she opened a book and began to study.
